      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear u, but the point of the character is that he's a \"bad\" comedian. if he just makes vague observations, he isn't the character we need for the skit. the satire comes from how cringe and offensive the jokes are. \n\ncould we at least try to just list some common tropes or archetypes for certain groups? like, just the \"labels\" or \"common assumptions\" people make about them? i don't need the full punchlines yet, i just need to know which specific stereotypes we're aiming to parody so i can structure the monologue around them. for example, if we're doing a bit on asian stereotypes or hispanic stereotypes, what are the most obvious ones we'd be mocking?",
